From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] quartz/vmr9: Create the default presenter's device
 multithreaded.

The default allocator-presenter's Direct3D 9 device is used from two
threads: the streaming thread presents each sample (PresentImage:
Clear, StretchRect, Present) and the application's thread repaints the
video (IVMRWindowlessControl9::RepaintVideo calls Present on the same
device, under the filter lock only). The device was created without
D3DCREATE_MULTITHREADED, so the two threads used it concurrently.
wined3d serializes every call itself; DXVK only does so for a
multithreaded device, and crashed on its command chunk swapped by the
other thread (a NULL chunk read in a Present).

Game impacted: Wasteland Racers 2071 (DND Arcade, Direct3D 8 under
DXVK) plays its attract movie in a windowless VMR-9 and calls
RepaintVideo every frame: the process crashed in DXVK's d3d9 after a
few seconds of the movie (11.7 s, at a random frame). With the patch the
movie plays to its end.

Create the device with D3DCREATE_MULTITHREADED.
---
--- a/dlls/quartz/vmr9.c
+++ b/dlls/quartz/vmr9.c
@@ -2488,7 +2488,8 @@
     d3dpp.BackBufferHeight = info->dwHeight;

     hr = IDirect3D9_CreateDevice(This->d3d9_ptr, d3d9_adapter, D3DDEVTYPE_HAL,
-            NULL, D3DCREATE_MIXED_VERTEXPROCESSING, &d3dpp, &device);
+            NULL, D3DCREATE_MIXED_VERTEXPROCESSING | D3DCREATE_MULTITHREADED,
+            &d3dpp, &device);
     if (FAILED(hr))
     {
         ERR("Failed to create device, hr %#lx.\n", hr);
